# Release and integration gates

Run the applicable checks before commit, merge to `main`, or a release tag.
Skip a check only when it cannot apply, and say so.

## Required as applicable

- Focused tests for the changed behavior
- `PYTHONPATH=src pytest -q`
- `python -m compileall -q src`
- `git diff --check`
- `node --check frontend/app.js` and `node --test frontend/app.test.mjs` when
  frontend changed
- Live-provider smoke testing when provider semantics changed
- Restart persistence testing when durable state changed
- Documentation audit against `README.md`, `AGENTS.md`, and `docs/`
- No Blocking or Important Reviewer findings
- Secrets and local SQLite state excluded from Git
- Accurate versioning (`pyproject.toml`, tags, docs)
- Clean Git state on the integration branch

Do not present the system as guaranteed financial advice. Do not tag a release
that weakens approval, HOLD, provenance, or managed/benchmark separation.
